WEBVTT

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.670
You can't come back because you're snowed in?

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.600
That's right.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.570
They said even the trains aren't running.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.440
It's such a bummer.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.480
You sound pretty happy for someone who's supposed to be bummed.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.670
<i>Sorry.</i>

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.970
<i>We'll be back by daytime tomorrow, okay?</i>

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.600
<i>Don't forget to lock up!</i>

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.600
Yeah, whatever.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.360
And a happy new year to you, too!

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.400
While <i>somebody</i> is out celebrating New Year's at the hot springs, I'm stuck—

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.490
What now?

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:42.370
<i>I hope you haven't forgotten.</i>

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.480
Damn that Akaishi.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.320
Training on New Year's Eve?

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.460
Just how strict is he?

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.490
Are you sure you're going to be all right, Aoba?

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.840
For the last time, I'll be fine.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.670
The hospitals are closed for the year-end holidays, you know.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.250
I got it, okay?

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.810
I won't let Momiji out of her bed no matter what.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.950
Ko!

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.630
Hey, you guys. Going somewhere?

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:47.510
Yes.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.760
Granny's sick in bed with a temperature, so we're going to go help her out.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.660
Oh, do you mean that granny we used to visit?

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:56.590
Oh yeah, you used to come visit her with us way back when, huh?

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:59.160
A New Year's Eve nightmare, huh?

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.430
Aren't you guys missing one person?

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.550
Momiji actually came down with a touch of a cold.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.530
Of course we can't take her with us, but I'm also worried about just leaving her here.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:12.040
Isn't that why we decided that I should stay and look after her?

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.140
But still...

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.780
There's nothing to worry about!

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.180
Say, Ko?

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.720
Could you come check up on these two when you're free?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.920
Don't tell me you trust this guy more than your own sister?!

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.840
I can take care of Momiji by myself.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:27.990
Aoba.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.830
Well...

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.560
We got to get going now!

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.910
Coming!

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:35.040
See you, Aoba.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.750
I'm counting on you, okay?

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.270
Have a happy new year, Ko!

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.150
So about Momiji...

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.150
Happy New Year!

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.090
Her cold...

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.190
Can I ask you something?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.960
What's this "secret weapon" business all about?

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.660
What are you trying to make me do?

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.570
I mean, don't you think you've put your hopes a little too high on me?

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.440
I'm not the only one who's pinned their hopes on you.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.380
Nakanishi.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.520
Hey.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.470
Doesn't this count as breaking and entering?

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:32.940
Don't worry.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.460
No one's going to be here on New Year's Eve.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.000
You think so?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.400
I've been wanting to get a feel for the high school's practice field.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:47.120
The three of us can play baseball here starting next spring, huh?

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.680
Ow!

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.720
Did you hear about the baseball transfer students?

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.330
The gist of it, yeah.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:18.640
They're apparently trying to put together a Koshien-worthy team

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.590
by recruiting promising players from all over the country.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.840
You think there will be spots for us on a team like that?

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.880
If there aren't any, we'll just make them.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.780
You said it.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.140
What's wrong?

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.980
Hey, didn't you say that there wasn't supposed to be anyone here today?

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.230
Yeah, what about it?

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.160
Well, there is definitely someone.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.960
That's the high school team coach!

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.850
Oh crap.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.230
H-Hello...

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:54.620
We're so sorry!

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.340
It's been too long.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.780
It truly has been too long.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.580
I haven't witnessed such a delightful practice in a long time.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.420
It almost feels like I've had my first dream of the year already.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.170
It's so cold!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.070
Come on, Momiji!

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:29.840
You need to stay in bed!

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.910
It's okay, I feel fine now.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.780
You're going to get a fever if you aren't careful.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:36.930
But Nomo's gone!

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.480
She'll probably find her own way home eventually.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.940
You're going to stay put now, okay?

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.360
I'll make you my special porridge in the meantime.

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:57.570
Hey, guys!

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:01.640
Hello.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.980
So she was with Ko!

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.560
We ran into each other, didn't we?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:06.560
Meow!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.310
How kind of you to bring her back.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:10.080
Don't mention it.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.690
Now if there's nothing else, could you kindly leave?

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.250
We're busy preparing for New Year's.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.740
I thought you'd be, so I bought you guys a few things.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:22.030
You sure are thoughtful, Ko!

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:26.100
My parents are over at some hot springs, so I'm dying of boredom.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.430
Then you can spend the night here!

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:30.400
What?! Don't be ridiculous!

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.500
In a house with only two girls home alone?

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.110
No way! Ko's spending the night.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:35.820
Momiji!

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.910
He's going to make my porridge, too!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.650
Your porridge would probably make me even sicker!

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:44.410
Okay, I'm on it.

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:49.520
All right then, have it your way.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:52.380
Make your cold worse and die! See if I care!

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.140
Could I borrow your pot?

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.810
Just grab whichever one you want from the kitchen.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.110
Thanks.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.480
Oh, but before that...

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:28.530
Sorry.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:30.930
I'm sorry, Momiji.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:33.200
Ko's really dependable, you know.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.570
Let's all eat his cooking together, okay?

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:39.330
Thanks.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:40.800
But...

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.400
I'll cook my own meal myself.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:53.450
New Year's soba noodles?

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:57.810
Bug off.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:58.720
All right then.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:04.190
Put a lot of ginger into that porridge, okay?

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.350
I was going to use spring onion.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.000
Nope, it's got to be ginger. It just has to be.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.010
And don't forget the egg at the end, okay?

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:14.170
Also, seed the pickled plum,
and dilute it with miso.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.210
You sure are picky, aren't you?

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.830
So that's the cookbook you were using.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:24.480
Let's see.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:25.620
No!

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.390
Don't read it without asking.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.500
What, Nomo?

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.160
I already gave you milk, didn't I?

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:46.100
You just sit tight here with Momiji.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:52.340
Your kettle's whistling, you know.

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.710
What should I do?

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.390
You really don't know?

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:58.820
Why don't I tell you.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.850
First you have to open the cover,

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:03.170
and pour hot water to the designated line inside.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.120
After you let it sit for three minutes, it—

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:26.950
Medicine!

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:32.930
Ice!

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.280
Bring me all the ice you have.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:39.870
Let me see it.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.590
Let's cool her head and her sides down with this, and see where it goes from there.

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:50.390
Grab some pajamas she can change into in case she starts sweating.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:32.900
Are you okay, Aoba?

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.750
This kind of fever won't kill me.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.140
What should I do?

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:40.610
Ichiyo said she'd be coming home late,

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:42.120
and Dad's...

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.340
I'm fine, Waka.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:45.810
I'm totally fine.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.430
I present to you my special porridge!

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:05.870
That cookbook I bought the other day sure came in handy.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.290
Open wide.

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:15.380
How is it?

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:17.540
It's good.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.810
Thank goodness.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.290
Come on, Aoba.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.760
But don't you usually get mad?

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.660
Today's a special case.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.910
You're so warm, Waka.

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.630
W-What?

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.530
The porridge is ready.

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:00.760
But Momiji's still...

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.740
We'll eat instead.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:03.720
Aren't you hungry?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:09.030
I added the ginger and eggs like you asked.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:13.270
Wow, it's good.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.700
You have to admit it's pretty good, right?

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.400
Oh, come on.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.210
You don't have to mean it, but at least tell me it tastes all right.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:27.750
It tastes the same.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.880
N-Nothing.

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:38.090
<i>It's just like what Waka made.</i>

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:42.290
No fair, you two!

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:44.640
Momiji! Are you okay?

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:46.000
Yup!

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:49.500
Looks like her fever's gone.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.940
I'm actually dying of hunger.

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:54.500
Hold on. I'll whip something up for you in a jiffy.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.820
Make some New Year's soba, too, while you're at it!

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.550
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:13:58.940
Soba for three, coming right up!

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.880
I don't want any.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.820
For two, then.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:18.580
How is it?

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:20.230
Peace!

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:23.200
Thank goodness.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.490
Hey, Ao,

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:28.380
I had this dream while I was sleeping just now.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:33.140
I dreamed about when I was in kindergarten and Waka was still around.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.180
I'm home!

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.640
Thank you so much for bringing her back every time.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.600
No worries. It's on our way home, anyway.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.910
See you tomorrow, Momiji!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.120
Bye bye!

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:50.130
Hey, Ichiyo, guess what I did today—

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.130
Excuse me, could we get two coffees?

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:52.270
Coming!

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:54.510
Come on and get changed.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:57.270
There's some shortcake in the fridge if you're hungry, okay?

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.810
Waka, Ao!

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:09.250
Your clothes are way too dirty, Aoba!

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.400
Who cares.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.950
It just shows how active I am.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:16.680
Even guys your age wouldn't have clothes <i>this</i> muddy.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.620
I'm gonna have to hand-wash these stains!

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.590
Geez!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.270
Hey.

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:37.380
Mah said her family's going to eat Korean barbecue today.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.480
That's cool.

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:44.810
Mah's my best friend whose family runs the bookstore.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.420
Oh really?

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.600
I like sushi better than Korean barbecue, though.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:58.210
In kindergarten today, we all drew pictures and mine was picked as the best one.

00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:01.070
Whoa! That's impressive.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:07.850
The teacher took a few pictures and asked everyone which one they liked best.

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:09.840
And what did you draw?

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.510
My mommy.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.480
Everyone was probably just being nice.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.280
She's not here, either!

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:30.860
Where did she go?

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:35.230
And Dad just has to be out drinking somewhere every time something like this happens...

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.500
I'm home!

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.160
Momiji!

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.270
Where in the world were you—

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:42.710
Hi.

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:47.020
What in the world were you thinking?

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:47.020
Ow.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.230
Do you know what time it is?

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:50.840
Could you not touch me there?

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:51.850
Ow...

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:52.650
Ow?

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.720
If you'll excuse me now.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:02.890
Ko listened to so many things I told him!

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:06.600
But after that we went over to the park and played pro wrestling!

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:09.430
He pretended to roll after I hit him with my flying kick,

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:12.540
and he bumped into the concrete in the sandpit here and there.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:21.110
Ko really is a good, reliable man.

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:25.790
Hey! Your fever's going to come back if you keep saying cheeky things like that.

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:41.390
What are you doing?

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:43.360
Go stay with Momiji for me.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.570
I'm just not cut out for it.

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:50.640
I can't become a good sister like Waka was.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.560
You're probably much better than—

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.850
That's not true.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:01.090
You're not that bad.

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.450
So you're saying I <i>am</i> bad, then?

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.130
Ow!

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:11.830
It's so good!

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.050
Yup.

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:15.770
Much better than instant noodles, I bet.

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:18.340
Instant noodles are delicious in their own way, you know.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:21.270
<i>There's not much left to the year now,</i>

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:24.680
<i>and I'm surrounded by an eager crowd of—</i>

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.680
Bravo!

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.210
Could you two keep it down?
I'm trying to watch TV.

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:34.350
Yay! Ao's the joker!

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:40.790
You have to pick this one!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.200
Let me take another one!

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.630
I said no!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:47.350
Don't you care about sportsmanship?

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.940
That's a totally different thing.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:49.910
What the hell?

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:09.190
Waka...

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:21.900
You're so warm, Waka.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:41.690
What's it say?

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.740
Back to normal!

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.030
That's good.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:49.060
I'm going to make some ozoni for you guys and head back home, then.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:52.500
You two looked pretty cute together there.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.860
She'll yell at you again if you say that, silly.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:59.640
Make some ozoni for Ao too, okay?

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:07.900
New Year's Day, huh?

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:08.680
Hey.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:11.780
You're awake.

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:14.420
Hey... Thanks for helping out.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:15.420
My pleasure.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:20.260
Judging by that bag, I guess it's really true that you're training.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:21.170
Huh?

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:23.010
Senda told me the other day.

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.010
That you started boxing or something.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:28.890
Oh... I guess that's the story for now.

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:29.780
See ya.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:41.670
All right!

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.960
I'm going to enjoy my lazy New Year's Day!

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:46.790
In your dreams, you are.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.520
Damn you!

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:57.600
Give me back my lazy New Year's Day!

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:02.060
April's going to creep up on you fast
if you keep zoning out like that.

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:13.260
Why did you join the baseball team?

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:15.310
To play baseball, of course.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:19.110
You portables better make those balls sparkle for the first-stringers!

00:23:19.110 --> 00:23:20.040
"Portables"?

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:23.950
You second-stringers are the definition of "portable"
since you don't have your own club room or practice field.

00:23:23.950 --> 00:23:24.920
Right, Azuma?

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:26.880
Who are you?

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:31.440
<i>Next time, on Cross Game Episode Six:</i>

00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:33.190
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:37.430
I can't remember the faces of people who aren't good for anything.
